  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "How many complex numbers satisfy the equation \\(z^5=\\overline{z},\\) where \\(\\overline{z}\\) is the conjugate of the complex number \\(z?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(5\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(6\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(7\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": "7"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2023-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Taking magnitudes gives \\(|z|^5=|z|,\\) so \\(|z|=0\\) or \\(|z|=1.\\) The value \\(z=0\\) works, giving one solution.\n\nIf \\(|z|=1,\\) multiply the equation by \\(z\\) to get \\(z^6=z\\overline{z}=|z|^2=1.\\) This has \\(6\\) distinct roots, all of modulus \\(1.\\)\n\nAltogether there are \\(1+6=7\\) solutions.\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Take absolute values: \\(|z|^5=|z|,\\) so \\(|z|=0\\) or \\(|z|=1\\)",
        "Multiplying by \\(z\\) gives \\(z^6=z\\overline{z}=|z|^2;\\) handle \\(z=0\\) separately"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
